FinDraft

Cursor AI Rules & Development Guide v3.2

Paste into .cursorrules and use as system prompts for Cursor AI / Claude Sonnet

Date: 29 August 2026 | Version: 3.2

Status: Supersedes v3.1

Revision Note

v3.1 fixed one internal disagreement found during independent review: Section 7.1's model-selection list only named GPT-4o-mini for the mapping tie-breaker, while Section 7.3 separately said to use it for "all non-critical tasks (mapping, risk explanations)" — leaving risk-explanation routing ambiguous. Section 7.1 now explicitly includes risk explanations. v3.2 syncs this document with Product Specification v3.2, which added an Irish legal/compliance section (archived_records table, a corrected TB-balance trigger, DPA/sub-processor requirements, EU data residency). Section 17's schema summary now includes archived_records, and Section 2's Privacy by Design principle and Section 14.1's environment table both note the EU-residency requirement that Product Spec Section 12.1 states explicitly.

1. Project Identity

FinDraft is a financial intelligence platform for accounting practices. Users upload trial balances (Excel/CSV) and receive auto-generated SOPL, SOFP, SOCIE, variance analysis with AI commentary, and risk flags. All financial calculations must be deterministic, auditable, and accurate to the penny.

Golden Rule: Python does the math. LLM does the narrative. Never the reverse.

2. Architectural Principles (Non-Negotiable)

-   Deterministic Math: All financial calculations use Python's Decimal module. NEVER use float for money. Tolerance: €0.01 (or functional currency equivalent).

-   AI-Narrative Separation: LLM generates text commentary only. LLM NEVER calculates, sums, or compares numbers. All numbers come from Python.

-   Evidence Graph: Every statement figure must be traceable to source TB rows. Store provenance metadata (source_account_ids).

-   Async by Default: All I/O operations (file upload, DB queries, LLM calls, export generation) use async/await.

-   Type Safety: All Python functions have type hints. All API inputs/outputs use Pydantic v2 models. Run mypy --strict in CI.

-   Fail Secure: If LLM fails, statements still generate without commentary. If validation fails, block export. Never show incorrect data.

-   No Raw Numbers in LLM Prompts: LLM prompts contain account names, variance directions, and percentage changes ONLY. Never include £/€/$ amounts, absolute values, or account balances.

-   Client Isolation: All data scoped to client_id and org_id. Row-level security enforced at BOTH application layer AND database layer (PostgreSQL RLS).

-   Defence in Depth: Security controls at multiple layers: auth, application, database, infrastructure.

-   Privacy by Design: GDPR compliance built-in. Minimise data collection. Encrypt at rest and in transit. Audit all access. Primary data (database AND file storage) hosted in an EU region — see Product Spec Section 12.1.

